string getFinishingItems(string payloadJson)
{
	// The finishing queue for one SUPERVISOR: every inspected batch that still
	// owes finishing, across every plan he owns, whether nobody has touched it or
	// somebody is part way through.
	//
	// IT USED TO TAKE A PLAN NUMBER, AND THAT WAS THE WRONG QUESTION. The floor
	// does not work a plan at a time - finishing is per BATCH, and batches arrive
	// from checking one at a time while other lines of the same order are still
	// being cut. Making the finisher pick a plan first meant he had to already
	// know which plan the pile in front of him came from, and a batch on a plan he
	// had not selected was invisible. The supervisor is the unit every other
	// screen in this app filters by, so it is the unit here too.
	//
	// THE SUPERVISOR IS Production_Planning.Assigned_To, resolved exactly the way
	// getPackingQueue resolves it - createProductionPlans stamps it, and the store
	// list, the receive screen and production all read it from there. Nothing
	// downstream of checking carries a supervisor of its own, so the plan is the
	// only route to one.
	//
	// NO SUPERVISOR MEANS AN EMPTY QUEUE, NEVER EVERYTHING. An unfiltered read
	// here would put every open batch in the building in front of whoever loaded
	// the screen before the picker settled, and two finishers would start the same
	// pile. A missing id is a screen that has not finished loading, not a request
	// for all work.
	//
	// ONE CARD PER Item_Check, AND NO GROUPING. The widget used to merge every
	// check sharing an item NAME into a single card and submit them together. A
	// remake batch repeats its original's name and SKU, and an alteration batch
	// has its name scrubbed of the "(Alteration Batch)" suffix below, so what
	// merged was three physically separate piles that arrived on different days -
	// and every Finishing_Data row they produced was then stamped with one
	// identical set of times. The durations were fiction.
	//
	// Item_Check is one record per BATCH, which is exactly one pile of garments
	// inspected together. That is the grain the floor works at, so that is the
	// grain of a card.
	//
	// AN OPEN JOB COMES BACK WITH ITS TIMES. status "In_Progress" plus whatever
	// sub-stage stamps exist, so a refresh, a closed tab or a handover to the next
	// shift resumes where the last person stopped instead of offering the batch as
	// untouched.
	//
	// "FINISHED" IS Finishing_Status == "Done", not "a row exists". Done means
	// done; anything else means the job is still open and resumable. Six functions
	// ask this question and they must all ask the same one - written this way
	// round so a row carrying neither value stays ON the queue, where somebody can
	// see it, rather than vanishing as finished work.
	//
	// Finishing_Data IS READ ONCE, FOR THE WHOLE QUEUE. The version this replaces
	// ran a Finishing_Data query per batch, which was survivable while the queue
	// was one plan and is not now that it is every plan a supervisor has ever
	// owned. One pass builds both the finished set and, for the open rows, the
	// row id and its six stamps - so the loop below is query-free on that side.
	// The statement-execution limit is NOT catchable: it kills the script and the
	// widget gets a bare 500 with no error card.
	//
	// STILL UNBOUNDED, deliberately and on the record: this reads the whole of
	// Finishing_Data, and it queries Item_Check once per plan the supervisor has
	// ever been given - including plans whose orders shipped months ago. Same debt
	// docs/scaling.md lists elsewhere. The real fix is a finishing marker on the
	// plan, or a date bound; filtering the plans by Order_Status was considered and
	// left alone, because a plan sitting on the wrong status would then hide real
	// work with nothing on screen to say so.

	res = "{\"errors\":[\"Nothing ran\"]}";

	try
	{
		raw = ifnull(payloadJson,"").toString().trim();

		if(raw == "")
		{
			return "{\"errors\":[],\"queue\":[]}";
		}

		inp = raw.toMap();
		supIdTxt = ifnull(inp.get("supervisorId"),"").toString().trim();

		if(supIdTxt == "" || supIdTxt.isNumber() == false)
		{
			return "{\"errors\":[],\"queue\":[]}";
		}

		supId = supIdTxt.toLong();

		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		// ONE PASS OVER Finishing_Data: which batches are finished, and for
		// the ones still open, the row to resume and the stamps it carries.
		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		// Keyed by Item_Check id as a STRING. Finishing_Data.Item_Check is a
		// lookup holding a record id while ID is a long, and comparing them
		// as-is is a mixed-type comparison, which throws rather than
		// returning false.
		doneChecks = List();
		openIdByCheck = Map();
		foldStartByCheck = Map();
		foldEndByCheck = Map();
		pressStartByCheck = Map();
		pressEndByCheck = Map();
		brandStartByCheck = Map();
		brandEndByCheck = Map();

		// THE PASS THAT USED TO BE HERE READ THE WHOLE FORM.
		//
		// It walked every Finishing_Data row ever written to fill these seven
		// maps. The form grows one row per inspected batch for ever, and the
		// statement-execution limit is NOT catchable - it kills the script, so
		// the finisher would have got a bare HTTP 500 with no error card.
		//
		// The maps are filled one check at a time now, at the point each check
		// is reached below, with the body of that pass moved there UNCHANGED -
		// same Done test in code, same else branch, same puts. fdSeen records
		// which checks have been asked about, so a check reached twice is read
		// once and a check with no Finishing_Data row at all is not re-queried.
		fdSeen = List();

		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		// His plans, with their plan number and order number resolved once
		// each - both are the same for every batch on a plan, and fetching
		// them per batch was two queries to learn something already known.
		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		planKeys = List();
		planNoByPlan = Map();
		soNoByPlan = Map();

		// sort by on its own assignment, never inline in a for each header.
		// Oldest plan first, so the longest-waiting work is at the top.
		myPlans = Production_Planning[Assigned_To == supId] sort by Added_Time;

		for each  pl in myPlans
		{
			planKeyTxt = pl.ID.toString();
			planKeys.add(planKeyTxt);
			planNoByPlan.put(planKeyTxt,ifnull(pl.Plan_No,"").toString().replaceAll("\"","'"));

			soTxt = "";

			if(pl.Sales_Order != null)
			{
				for each  so in Sales_Order[ID == pl.Sales_Order]
				{
					soTxt = ifnull(so.Sales_Order,"").toString().replaceAll("\"","'");
				}
			}

			soNoByPlan.put(planKeyTxt,soTxt);
		}

		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		// The batches. Item name and SKU are cached per Plan_Item and filled
		// in the first time a batch actually needs them, because many checks
		// point at one item - a root, its remake and its alteration batch all
		// name the same Plan_Item. itemsSeen records WHICH ids have been
		// resolved: an item with no name resolves to "", which a Map cannot
		// tell apart from an id never looked up, so without it every such
		// item is re-queried on every batch it owns.
		//------------------------------------------------------------------
		nameByItem = Map();
		skuByItem = Map();
		itemsSeen = List();

		rowsJson = "";

		for each  planKeyOne in planKeys
		{
			// sort by on its own assignment, never inline in a for each
			// header. Oldest batch first within the plan, matching the order
			// checking released them in.
			checks = Item_Check[Plan == planKeyOne.toLong() && Qty_Approved > 0] sort by Added_Time;

			for each  chk in checks
			{
				chkKey = chk.ID.toString();

				// PROCESSED IS THE "CHECKING IS FINISHED WITH IT" MARKER, and it
				// is the gate here.
				//
				// saveItemCheck inserts the Item_Check with Processed = false and
				// sets it true as its very last statement, once every record that
				// check owed exists - the remake batch, the alteration batch,
				// their requirements. A check sitting at Processed = false is one
				// that died part way through: the approved figure is on the record
				// but the batches it should have created may not be.
				//
				// Offering it for finishing would put a pile of garments on the
				// floor before checking had finished deciding what happens to the
				// rest of them. Cheap test, and it is the one saveItemCheck's own
				// header names as the pair to look for.
				chkDone = ifnull(chk.Processed,false);

				//------------------------------------------------------
				// THIS CHECK'S FINISHING ROW, read once. The body below is
				// the old whole-form pass, moved here and scoped to one
				// check - see the note where fdSeen is declared.
				//------------------------------------------------------
				if(fdSeen.contains(chkKey) == false)
				{
					fdSeen.add(chkKey);

					for each  fd in Finishing_Data[Item_Check == chk.ID]
					{
						if(ifnull(fd.Finishing_Status,"").toString().trim() == "Done")
						{
							doneChecks.add(chkKey);
						}
						else
						{
							// startFinishingJob reuses any non-Done row rather
							// than adding a second one next to it, so there is
							// at most one open row per batch and this put
							// cannot fight itself.
							openIdByCheck.put(chkKey,fd.ID.toString());

							if(fd.Folding_Start_Time != null)
							{
								foldStartByCheck.put(chkKey,fd.Folding_Start_Time.toString());
							}
							if(fd.Folding_End_Time != null)
							{
								foldEndByCheck.put(chkKey,fd.Folding_End_Time.toString());
							}
							if(fd.Pressing_Start_Time != null)
							{
								pressStartByCheck.put(chkKey,fd.Pressing_Start_Time.toString());
							}
							if(fd.Pressing_End_Time != null)
							{
								pressEndByCheck.put(chkKey,fd.Pressing_End_Time.toString());
							}
							if(fd.Branding_Start_Time != null)
							{
								brandStartByCheck.put(chkKey,fd.Branding_Start_Time.toString());
							}
							if(fd.Branding_End_Time != null)
							{
								brandEndByCheck.put(chkKey,fd.Branding_End_Time.toString());
							}
						}
					}
				}

				if(doneChecks.contains(chkKey) == false && chkDone == true)
				{
					itemKeyTxt = "";

					if(chk.Plan_Item != null)
					{
						itemKeyTxt = chk.Plan_Item.toString();
					}

					if(itemKeyTxt != "" && itemsSeen.contains(itemKeyTxt) == false)
					{
						itemsSeen.add(itemKeyTxt);
						nameByItem.put(itemKeyTxt,"");
						skuByItem.put(itemKeyTxt,"");

						for each  pi in Plan_Item[ID == itemKeyTxt.toLong()]
						{
							// The suffix is scrubbed so an alteration batch
							// reads as the product the finisher recognises.
							// It does NOT merge it with anything - the
							// batches stay separate cards.
							nameClean = ifnull(pi.Item_Name,"").toString();
							nameClean = nameClean.replaceAll("(Alteration Batch)","");
							nameClean = nameClean.replaceAll("(alteration batch)","");
							nameClean = nameClean.replaceAll("Alteration Batch","");
							nameClean = nameClean.replaceAll("alteration batch","");
							nameByItem.put(itemKeyTxt,nameClean.replaceAll("\"","'").trim());

							// Item_Sku is a LOOKUP holding a record id, not
							// the SKU text, so it has to be resolved through
							// the master or the screen shows an 18-digit id.
							skuTxt = "";

							for each  imRec in Item_Master[ID == pi.Item_Sku]
							{
								skuTxt = ifnull(imRec.SKU,"").toString().replaceAll("\"","'");
							}

							skuByItem.put(itemKeyTxt,skuTxt);
						}
					}

					itemName = ifnull(nameByItem.get(itemKeyTxt),"").toString();
					skuOut = ifnull(skuByItem.get(itemKeyTxt),"").toString();

					// An open row hands back its id and its stamps so the
					// operator resumes; a batch nobody has touched has no row
					// yet, so finishingId is 0 and startFinishingJob opens
					// one on the first press.
					finIdOut = ifnull(openIdByCheck.get(chkKey),"0").toString();
					finStatus = "Pending";

					if(finIdOut != "0")
					{
						finStatus = "In_Progress";
					}

					if(rowsJson != "")
					{
						rowsJson = rowsJson + ",";
					}

					// Ids stringified - an 18-digit id breaks JSON.parse on
					// the widget side.
					rowsJson = rowsJson + "{\"id\":\"" + chkKey + "\","
						+ "\"finishingId\":\"" + finIdOut + "\","
						+ "\"planItemId\":\"" + itemKeyTxt + "\","
						+ "\"salesOrder\":\"" + ifnull(soNoByPlan.get(planKeyOne),"").toString() + "\","
						+ "\"planNo\":\"" + ifnull(planNoByPlan.get(planKeyOne),"").toString() + "\","
						+ "\"itemName\":\"" + itemName + "\","
						+ "\"sku\":\"" + skuOut + "\","
						+ "\"qty\":" + ifnull(chk.Qty_Approved,0).toLong() + ","
						+ "\"status\":\"" + finStatus + "\","
						+ "\"stages\":{"
						+ "\"folding\":{\"start\":\"" + ifnull(foldStartByCheck.get(chkKey),"").toString() + "\",\"end\":\"" + ifnull(foldEndByCheck.get(chkKey),"").toString() + "\"},"
						+ "\"pressing\":{\"start\":\"" + ifnull(pressStartByCheck.get(chkKey),"").toString() + "\",\"end\":\"" + ifnull(pressEndByCheck.get(chkKey),"").toString() + "\"},"
						+ "\"branding\":{\"start\":\"" + ifnull(brandStartByCheck.get(chkKey),"").toString() + "\",\"end\":\"" + ifnull(brandEndByCheck.get(chkKey),"").toString() + "\"}"
						+ "}}";
				}
			}
		}

		res = "{\"errors\":[],\"queue\":[" + rowsJson + "]}";
	}
	catch (e)
	{
		res = "{\"errors\":[\"DELUGE: " + e.toString().replaceAll("\"","'") + "\"]}";
	}

	return res;
}
